Jesus Heals a Paralyzed Man (Matthew 9:1-8; Luke 5:17-26)
And after a few days, Jesus returned to the region of Capernaum, and the news spread that he was in the house.
A lot of people gathered until there was no space left for anyone in front of the door. He began to tell them about the word of God.
And they brought a paralyzed man, carried by four men.
But they couldn't get close because of the large crowd. So they dug through the roof of the house where Jesus was and lowered the mat on which the paralyzed man was lying.
When Jesus saw their faith, he said to the paralyzed man, "Son, your sins are forgiven."
And there was a group of the People of the Book, some of the Jewish merchants, who began to think within their hearts:
"Does a man like this talk like that? He is blaspheming! Who but God alone can forgive sins?"
And at the time, Jesus knew what they were thinking and asked them: "Why are you thinking about this?"
Is it easier for Anna? To say to the paralyzed person: "Your sins are forgiven" or to say to him: "Get up! Take your bed and walk."
But this way you will know that the Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins." Then he said to the paralyzed man:
